{
    // Bond Asset Vault - May be spent with the bond asset, as long as the asset is burned.
    // Every bond pays its repayment or liquidated collateral here, and whoever holds the bond asset claims
    // it. The asset is the bearer claim on the bond.
    // One vault serves every bond: it has no constants, so every bond names the same hash.
    //
    // REGISTERS
    // R4: Coll[Byte] - Box id of the bond this box settles. Not read here; the bond pinned it.
    // R5: Coll[Byte] - Token Id of bond asset that claims this box. The bond pinned it to the asset its R4 names.
    //
    // ASSUMPTIONS
    // - The bond asset came from a verified mint, so its supply is exactly 1 and the lender holds it.
    //   Only one unit can ever be presented here.
    // - Anyone can send a box here naming any asset in R5. That only gives their own funds to whoever
    //   holds that asset; only boxes a bond created are worth anything, and the bond pins R5. A bond built
    //   by hand can name any asset too, and so only ever pays that asset's holder.
    // - Burning the asset is all-or-nothing: every vault box for this asset must be claimed in the
    //   same transaction. Anything sent here afterwards is locked for good.
    // - A box without a Coll[Byte] R5 is locked for good.
    // - The outputs are not constrained. The holder takes everything, wherever they like.
    // - A vault box holding its own bond asset is spendable by anyone. Never send the asset here.

    // Helper Methods
    def numTokenInOutputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        OUTPUTS.fold(0L, {
            (a: Long, b: Box) =>
                val totalTokens = b.tokens.fold(0L, {
                  (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => if(t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
                })
                a + totalTokens
        })
    }
    def numTokenInInputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        INPUTS.fold(0L, {
            (a: Long, b: Box) =>
                val totalTokens = b.tokens.fold(0L, {
                  (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) => if(t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
                })
                a + totalTokens
        })
    }
    val bondAssetId = SELF.R5[Coll[Byte]].get
    val assetSpent = numTokenInInputs(bondAssetId) >= 1
    val assetBurned = numTokenInOutputs(bondAssetId) == 0
    sigmaProp(assetSpent && assetBurned)
}
